<title>SWEDEN: Sweden's March current account surplus 4.4 bln Skr.</title>
<headline>Sweden's March current account surplus 4.4 bln Skr.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sweden's current account for March showed a surplus of 4.4 billion crowns for a surplus of 36.4 billion in the last 12 months, the central bank said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>    SWEDISH CURRENT ACCOUNT	 March 97   Feb 97   March 96</p>
<p>Monthly balance			   +4.4	+3.1	+4.3</p>
<p>Year/year				  +36.4     +36.3     +41.7</p>
<p>Note - Figures are in billions of crowns. Average market expectations had been for a 3.1 billion crown surplus in March.</p>
<p>-- Birgitta Forsberg, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1017</p>
